/* ============================================================================
   words-5.js — the five-letter dictionary used to VALIDATE a guess.

   This is deliberately separate from the answers. A puzzle's answer is drawn
   from a short curated list of everyday words, because nobody wants to be
   told the solution was an obscurity. What you are ALLOWED to guess is a far
   wider net, because being told CRANE or SLATE "is not a word" is the fastest
   way to make a word game feel broken. Wordle draws the same distinction:
   roughly two thousand answers against thirteen thousand accepted guesses.

   Every entry is exactly five letters, so they are stored end to end with no
   separators and sliced apart on load — smaller than any delimited form, and
   there is nothing to parse.

   Source: dwyl/english-words (public domain), filtered to /^[a-z]{5}$/ and
   upper-cased. It is permissive by design: it carries proper nouns and
   archaic spellings, which is the right bias for a validator. See the note in
   the handover about an editorial pass before this goes public.
   ========================================================================= */
window.WORDS5 = "";
